MIT KEMAR HRTF measurements
Copyright 1994 by the MIT Media Laboratory.
Authors: Bill Gardner and Keith Martin.

This data is provided free with no restrictions on use, provided the authors
are cited when the data is used in any research or commercial application.

Source and original terms: https://sound.media.mit.edu/resources/KEMAR.html
Dataset: https://sound.media.mit.edu/resources/KEMAR/diffuse.zip
SHA-256: a48e73137390626ef1e45d1de6a4d98530c6aa570e71b40f7c4442241ed5fa22

Funke embeds the diffuse-field equalized, symmetric small-pinna measurements
(44.1 kHz, 128 samples per ear). The engine interpolates and resamples these
measurements for headphone playback. The data covers elevations -40 to +90
degrees; lower directions use the -40 degree measurements.
